# Bharat-OS Kernel Development - Cursor Rules

## Constitutional Authority
All Cursor agents must follow the repository constitution in [AGENTS.md](AGENTS.md).
Canonical domain skills are located in `.agents/skills/`.

## Context Pack First
Query compact subsystem metadata and assigned skills before planning:
```bash
python3 tools/agents/context_pack.py --area <area-name> --format compact
```

## Strict Architectural Requirements
- **Standard**: C23 (ISO/IEC 9899:2024). No standard library in kernel.
- **Layering**: Kernel = mechanisms only (`core/kernel/`); Services = policy (`core/services/`); HAL = contracts (`core/hal/`); Arch = ISA (`core/arch/`).
- **Capability-Mediated**: Every resource access requires a capability. Deny by default, fail closed.
- **Ownership**: Mutable state is core-local. Never access remote runqueues directly.
- **Wire Safety**: Fixed-width integers (`uint32_t`, `uint64_t`), compile-time assertions. No raw pointers across IPC/wire boundaries.
- **Bounded Timing**: Monotonic deadlines via `bh_ktime_now()`. No spin-counter loops.
- **Memory**: Support MMU_FULL, MMU_LITE, and MPU/PMP. Fail closed (`BH_STATUS_ERR_UNSUPPORTED`) on unsupported backends.
- **Usercopy**: Never dereference user pointers directly. Use fault-safe usercopy before inspecting fields or capability handles.

## Build & Validation
- Template source for kernel config is `core/kernel/include/bharat_config.h.in`. Never commit generated `bharat_config.h`.
- Verify changes with:
  ```bash
  python3 tools/agents/verify.py --changed-files <changed_files>
  python3 tools/run_qemu_matrix.py --headless --smoke --all-arch
  ```
- Never report unexecuted checks as PASS.
